Every line of a multi-line `--said` is blockquoted on its own, never reworded. The newline is
passed through `printf` under `sh`, since a `cmd` line cannot carry one.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  "core.macros.date +%Y-%m-%d %H:%M": "2026-10-15 15:40"
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p/index.md --
---
title: P
---

# P
-- cmd --
sh -c 'booping correction add --target plans/p/index.md --step groom/draft-plan --did "wrote one milestone" --said "$(printf "no.\nsplit it in two")" --why "too big"'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/p/corrections.md#R1
-- stderr --
warning: no session id; dialogue not linked
-- expected/cwd/vault/plans/p/corrections.md --
# Corrections

## R1 — groom/draft-plan — 2026-10-15 15:40

**Did:** wrote one milestone

**Said:**

> no.
> split it in two

**Why:** too big

**Dialogue:** not found — no session id

**Artifact:** [index.md](index.md)
